@*
 * FILE ROLE: Root _ViewStart.cshtml — sets the default layout for all views in the
 *   root Views/ folder (HomeController views). The Razor engine applies this file
 *   before rendering any view that doesn't set Layout = null or override the layout.
 *
 * _ViewStart.cshtml DISCOVERY FOR NON-AREA VIEWS:
 *   The engine applies _ViewStart.cshtml files hierarchically, most general first:
 *     1. _ViewStart.cshtml (project root)       — applied first
 *     2. Views/_ViewStart.cshtml                — applied second (this file)
 *     3. Views/Home/_ViewStart.cshtml           — applied last (if it existed)
 *   Each file can override Layout set by the previous. Individual views can
 *   override further with @{ Layout = null; } to opt out of any layout.
 *
 * "_Layout" RESOLUTION (from non-area views):
 *   The framework searches for _Layout.cshtml:
 *     1. Views/Home/_Layout.cshtml               — not found
 *     2. Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml             ← found (root layout)
 *   Non-area views always use the root Shared layout.
*@

@{
    Layout = "_Layout"; // resolved to Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml for non-area views
}
